  "proposals": [
    {
      "id": "106",
      "title": "Marketing Committee — Operations & Reddit Contributor Pilot",
      "summary": "The Gonka Marketing Committee requests 6,800 USDT + 50,000 GNK from the Community Pool to support ongoing Committee work and a separate two-month Reddit Contributor Pilot.\n\nThe Committee acts as a community-side contributor team supporting active marketing projects. Its work includes joining contractor calls, reviewing deliverables, tracking progress, and consolidating feedback from hosts and other contributors. The team has already been involved with TheSoul and Input, including reviews of Gonka positioning, the Brandbook, website wireframes, and other ongoing materials.\n\nThe proposal also includes a two-month Reddit pilot to test a more systematic community presence on the platform. This includes developing r/GonkaHub, bringing in contributors, identifying relevant communities, and supporting active participation.",
      "status": "VOTING_PERIOD",
      "votingStart": "2026-09-21T19:09:41.762006655Z",
      "votingEnd": "2026-09-23T19:09:41.762006655Z",
      "messages": [
        "/cosmwasm.wasm.v1.MsgExecuteContract",
        "/cosmos.distribution.v1beta1.MsgCommunityPoolSpend"
      ],
      "yes": "0",
      "no": "0",
      "abstain": "0"
    },
    {
      "id": "105",
      "title": "Approve devshard v5 and bounty payouts",
      "summary": "Approve DevShard v5 and contributor bounty payouts\n\nThis proposal adds DevShard v5 to the approved list of devshard versions and distributes 91,300 USDT from the community-sale contract to contributors.\n\nRelease was tested with core testteam and external testlab.\n\nDevShard v5 is the next protocol version after the v4 line. Its main protocol addition is height-sync, which gives DevShard sessions a signed, replayable view of mainnet height and establishes protocol-level logical time for future cPoC, timeout, dispute mechanisms and protocol-level QoS.\n\nThe release also includes high-availability improvements, warm cutover and session recovery, Gateway updates, validation and settlement fixes, security hardening, observability improvements and expanded end-to-end testing.\n\nThe bounty recipients are Gonka core-contributors who have been actively involved across multiple development cycles and releases:\n\n@akup / @a-kuprin — contributing since v0.2.6, and extensively across DevShard v3, v4 and v5.\n@qdanik — active since v0.2.11, including v0.2.14/v0.2.15 and DevShard/Gateway work.\n@Ryanchen911 — active since the v0.2.12 cycle, with contributions across chain, security and DevShard-related releases.\n@aikuznetsov — active through the DevShard v4 / v0.2.15 cycle, primarily on testing and protocol reliability.\n@snevolin — active since the DevShard v4 / v0.2.15 cycle, focused on high availability, routing and safe runtime upgrades.\n@shd — contributed to DevShard v4/v5 protocol review and formalization, including the height-sync design.\n@redstartechno — active since the v0.2.15 development cycle, contributing reliability and DevShard fixes.\n\nThe detailed technical scope, individual contributions, PR references and full bounty breakdown are available here: https://github.com/gonka-ai/gonka/pull/1584\n\nThe description: https://github.com/gonka-ai/gonka/blob/devshard-0.2.15-v5/proposals/governance-artifacts/update-v0.2.15-devshard-v5/README.md (sha256 7bba17188e4c3d15476f2c6330281b3908fc124e9eb26950acd6f9f927d89dc4)",
      "status": "PASSED",
      "votingStart": "2026-09-16T16:47:54.790005493Z",
      "votingEnd": "2026-09-18T16:47:54.790005493Z",
      "messages": [
        "/inference.inference.MsgUpdateParams",
