    {
      "id": "103",
      "title": "Reimbursement of Expenses for Daniil and David Liberman's Participation in All-In Summit 2026",
      "summary": "We are proposing to allocate 15,500 USDT from the Gonka Community Pool to reimburse the cost of two tickets for All-In Summit 2026 for Daniil and David Liberman, co-creators of the Gonka protocol.\nAll-In Summit will take place on September 13–15, 2026, in Los Angeles and will bring together more than 2,500 hand-selected attendees, including tech founders, investors, executives, and leaders from the AI industry.\nThe standard Attendee Pass costs $7,500 per person. The tickets have already been paid for. The requested reimbursement covers only the cost of the two tickets plus transaction fees for withdrawing the funds. Flights, accommodation, and any other expenses are not being requested from the Community Pool under this proposal.",
      "status": "PASSED",
      "votingStart": "2026-09-10T13:31:12.594032166Z",
      "votingEnd": "2026-09-12T13:31:12.594032166Z",
      "messages": [
        "/cosmwasm.wasm.v1.MsgExecuteContract"
      ],
      "yes": "184762",
      "no": "0",
      "abstain": "0"
    },
    {
      "id": "102",
      "title": "Ratify Quant Mesh Limited as the Ledger Integration Counterparty and Fund the Initial Ledger Integration Payment",
      "summary": "6Block proposes that the Gonka community ratify and authorize Quant Mesh Limited as the legal contracting counterparty for the Gonka-Ledger integration and allocate 350,350 USDT from the Community Pool to Quant Mesh Limited at gonka1yqj5xf0wtqgpdmv5v68cus0tp2j5fv7lzcfd6g.\n\nThe allocation consists of 350,000 USDT for the initial Ledger integration payment (275,000 USDT Phase 1 Launch Fees and 75,000 USDT first-year Annual Activation Fee) plus 350 USDT for processing costs. This authorization and funding are strictly limited to the Ledger integration described in the full proposal.",
      "status": "PASSED",
      "votingStart": "2026-09-09T09:28:14.306648256Z",
      "votingEnd": "2026-09-11T09:28:14.306648256Z",
      "messages": [
        "/cosmwasm.wasm.v1.MsgExecuteContract"
      ],
      "yes": "146903",
      "no": "0",
      "abstain": "5568"
    },
    {
      "id": "101",
      "title": "Add GLM-5.3-Flash, remove Kimi-K2.6 and GLM-5.2-FP8 from PoC models",
      "summary": "Add zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash as a governance-approved model and PoC model. Remove moonshotai/Kimi-K2.6 and zai-org/GLM-5.2-FP8 from poc_params.models.\n\nMiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.7 and deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 are not affected: their PoC parameters and weights remain unchanged. All other chain parameters remain unchanged.\n\nThe GLM-5.3-Flash model and its parameters were proposed by the kaitaku.ai team, independently validated by vbgd0, and are now proposed jointly. Release inputs, measurements and the reasoning behind the thresholds are in gonka-ai/gonka#1734.\n\nGLM-5.3-Flash PoC parameters: seq_len 1024, dist_threshold 0.44, p_mismatch 0.10, p_value_threshold 0.05, weight_scale_factor 0.62; validation_threshold 0.951.\n\nThe weight_scale_factor was calibrated so that a B200 host switching its PoC model to GLM-5.3-Flash is expected to gain approximately 7% more weight relative to its current weight. For other GPUs the optimal model does not change.\n\nThe activation epoch (penalty_start_epoch) for GLM-5.3-Flash is 394.",
      "status": "PASSED",
      "votingStart": "2026-09-08T23:17:27.402122371Z",
      "votingEnd": "2026-09-10T23:17:27.402122371Z",
      "messages": [
        "/inference.inference.MsgUpdateParams",
        "/inference.inference.MsgRegisterModel"
      ],
      "yes": "309308",
      "no": "0",
      "abstain": "3168"
    },
    {
      "id": "100",
      "title": "devshard v4.1",
      "summary": "Add v4.1 to the approved list of devshard versions.",
      "status": "PASSED",
      "votingStart": "2026-09-08T22:36:34.311913031Z",
